WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:16.669
Registration connects a physical device to a record in your
fleet. It tells SuiFleet which device you manage, so updates and
reports can be associated with the right machine. Register by
address is useful for a small pilot or a single device you are
setting up.

2
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:32.696
Choose Register by address. Give the device a recognizable name,
then enter the public address generated by its edge client and
choose the matching architecture. The private key stays on the
device; this form only needs its public identity.

3
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:44.493
Review the details, then register the device and approve the
request. A useful name makes it easier to find the machine later
when targeting an update or investigating a failure.

4
00:00:45.200 --> 00:01:03.291
The device now appears in your inventory. Registration alone
does not install the client or prove the machine is online.
Health reports begin after its configured client starts and can
communicate. For manufacturing batches, use Enrollment instead
of entering every address manually.

